Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:36:23 +0800
Subject: dt-bindings: mtd: include the clock header the example uses

The clock id split left histb-clock.h as a forwarding shim that emits a
warning, and the dw-mshc example still includes it, so every
dt_binding_check run pays for that warning.

Include the CRG header of the SoC the example describes; the four clock
ids it takes already live there under the same HISTB_ names.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)


diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-dw-mshc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-dw-mshc.yaml
index e447579e0f22..02d79a8c6377 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-dw-mshc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-dw-mshc.yaml
@@ -71,7 +71,7 @@ unevaluatedProperties: false
 
 examples:
   - |
-    #include <dt-bindings/clock/histb-clock.h>
+    #include <dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798cv200-crg.h>
     #include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/arm-gic.h>
 
     mmc@9830000 {
